          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "comment": "Self-referencing: naming the gig this one repeats lets a repeat booking\ncarry its history forward without duplicating the earlier record.",
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Title",
            "targetObject": "Event"
          },
          "name": "PreviousGig",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "comment": "Matches `Band.CreatedBy` and `SetList.CreatedBy`: an explicit creator\nlookup, not just the automatic `_createdBy` metadata field, so a gig\nrecord names who booked it the same way its sibling objects do. Neither\nof those two shows up on its own create form either -- both are\npopulated by the write path itself (`CreateBand`'s command step, and a\ndirect field on `band-app.ts`'s seed calls for `SetList`); `Event` has no\ndedicated `CreateEvent` command, so it is populated the same way\n`SetList`'s already is: directly in `band-app.ts`'s seed calls.",
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Name",
            "targetObject": "User"
          },
          "name": "CreatedBy",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        }
