          "reorder": "shift",
          "scopeFields": [
            "Band"
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "giggle-new's `set_list_songs` carries `UNIQUE (set_list_id, song_id)`: the\nsame song cannot appear twice in one set list. `SongPicker`'s\n`EXCLUDE_LINKED` already hides an already-added song, but a picker that\ndeclines to offer a duplicate is a UI affordance, not enforcement -- nothing\nstopped a direct create or a replayed authority write from making one. This\nis the object constraint the real schema always had.",
          "fields": [
            "Song"
          ],
          "kind": "unique",
          "name": "uniqueSongInSetList",
          "scopeFields": [
            "SetList"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fields": [
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Name",
            "targetObject": "Band"
          },
          "name": "Band",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Name",
            "targetObject": "SetList"
          },
          "name": "SetList",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Title",
            "targetObject": "Song"
          },
          "name": "Song",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "name": "Position",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "number",
          "validators": [
            {
              "kind": "min",
              "value": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "A set-list item is not just a link to a song: how it is played, whether it\ncloses the night, and when it was last rehearsed all belong to the item.\nThese are what make the child collection's inline editor exercise the real\nfield renderer -- an enum, a boolean and a date beside the song lookup.",
          "defaultValue": "Full",
          "hidden": false,
          "name": "Arrangement",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": [
            {
              "kind": "in",
              "value": [
                "Full",
                "Acoustic",
                "Instrumental"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "defaultValue": false,
          "hidden": false,
          "name": "Encore",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "boolean",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
