    },
    {
      "comment": "The gig \u003c-\u003e set-list link, and the reason `Event` no longer carries a single\n`SetList` lookup. giggle-new's `gig_set_lists(gig_id, set_list_id, position)`\nis a genuine ordered many-to-many -- its production data has nights running\ntwo set lists in order, and its gig form lets an admin add, reorder and\ndetach them one at a time. Same shape as `SetListItem` one object up (an\n`ORDERED` position under a parent, a `UNIQUE` guard against linking the same\nchild twice), because it is the same kind of relationship: `SetListItem`\norders songs within a set list, `EventSetList` orders set lists within a\nnight.",
      "computedFields": [],
      "constraints": [
        {
          "compaction": "onDelete",
          "kind": "ordered",
          "name": "orderedEventSetLists",
          "parentField": "Event",
          "positionField": "Position",
          "reorder": "shift",
          "scopeFields": [
            "Band"
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "`gig_set_lists`' own primary key is `(gig_id, set_list_id)`: one set list\ncannot be attached to the same event twice.",
          "fields": [
            "SetList"
          ],
          "kind": "unique",
          "name": "uniqueSetListForEvent",
          "scopeFields": [
            "Event"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fields": [
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Name",
            "targetObject": "Band"
          },
          "name": "Band",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Title",
            "targetObject": "Event"
          },
          "name": "Event",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "lookup": {
            "displayField": "Name",
            "targetObject": "SetList"
          },
          "name": "SetList",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        },
        {
          "hidden": false,
          "name": "Position",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": true,
          "type": "number",
          "validators": [
            {
              "kind": "min",
              "value": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "comment": "Not a `gig_set_lists` column, but the thing its users write into the gig's\nshared `notes` field instead -- which set is the acoustic one, which one\nfollows the interval. Kept on the link rather than the set list because the\nsame set list is reused across nights.",
          "hidden": false,
          "name": "Notes",
          "readonly": false,
          "required": false,
          "type": "text",
          "validators": []
        }
      ],
