    {
      "comment": "A signed-in caller may resolve a musician's *name*, and nothing else.\n\n`FIELDS Name` is what makes that true rather than aspirational: a rule that\nnames `FIELDS` cannot match a whole-record request at all (`ruleMatches`,\n`policy-engine.ts`), so this grants the display field and never the record\nit lives on. `Email` has no rule of its own, so default deny applies to it,\nand there is deliberately no `SEARCH` rule -- search is the enumeration\nprimitive over a user directory, and once `CurrentUserAvailability` stopped\nsourcing `User` nothing legitimate needed it. `UserSystemAdminPolicy` above\nkeeps `SystemAdmin`'s whole-record access untouched.\n\nThis narrows the whole-object `ALLOW SEARCH/READ AUTHENTICATED` pair Phase\n91 put here, which was defensible only while registration was invite-only:\nevery authenticated caller had been vouched for by somebody already inside.\nPhase 99 adds self-service registration, so \"anyone who can reach the\nauthority may sign up\" plus \"any authenticated caller may read every `User`\nrecord\" would have been an open directory of every user's name and email.\n\nWhat must not come back is the *pre*-Phase-91 `ROLE BandMember` pair, which\nmatched nothing at all: a context-scoped `ROLE` condition only resolves\nagainst an object that is itself scoped to that context (`SCOPE Band FIELD\nBand`) or is a context's own bound object (`Band`, for `CONTEXT Band OBJECT\nBand`). `User` is neither -- it is the bound object of the *`User`* context\n-- so `getPolicyRequestContextTargets` (`context-scope.ts`) could only ever\nresolve a `User`-object check against the caller's own identity selection.\nThe compiler refuses that shape now (`ADL_POLICY_ROLE_PRINCIPAL_UNREACHABLE`,\nPhase 93).\n\nTwo narrower grants remain inexpressible and are not attempted here. \"Only\npeople I share a band with\" needs `CONTEXT_MEMBER` to key on a field holding\nthe record's own id, and a `User` record has none. \"My own record in full\"\nneeds the same thing: `OWNER` matches `meta.createdBy`/`CreatedBy`/`OwnerId`,\nnone of which a `User` record carries about itself, and no policy condition\ncan compare a record's id to `runtime.userId`.",
      "name": "UserPolicy",
      "object": "User",
      "rules": [
        {
          "action": "read",
          "effect": "allow",
          "fields": [
            "Name"
          ],
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedReadUserName",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "BandPolicy",
      "object": "Band",
      "rules": [
        {
          "action": "search",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandMemberSearchBands",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandMember"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandMemberReadBand",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandMember"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "create",
          "condition": "CreatedBy == RUNTIME.userId",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedCreateOwnBand",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "condition": "CreatedBy == RUNTIME.userId",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandCreatorReadOwnBand",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "update",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminUpdateBand",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "delete",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminDeleteBand",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "comment": "\"You have been invited to The Betas\" is the whole point of\n`MyBandInvitationList`, and without this rule the row reads\n`band-b4b935e2-...` instead: a `CONTEXT_GRANT` puts the *granted* object\n(`BandInvitation`) in reach of the object-scope gate and never the\ncontext's own root object, and no other `BandPolicy` rule fits a pending\ninvitee -- `allowBandMemberReadBand` wants the role they have not got and\n`allowBandCreatorReadOwnBand` wants a band they did not create. Jointly\nCare's `MyPendingCircleInvites` records the same finding and routes around\nit by not naming the circle at all; the mechanism that makes naming it\nsafe (Phase 101) landed after that comment was written.\n\n`FIELDS Name` is what makes this a field grant rather than a record grant:\na rule that names `FIELDS` cannot match a whole-record request at all\n(`ruleMatches`, `policy-engine.ts`), so `runtime.read('Band', ...)` stays\ndenied for an invitee and `Description`, `Biography` and the social links\nkeep their own default deny. Same construction as `UserPolicy.\nallowAuthenticatedReadUserName` above -- see its comment for the fuller\naccount of why the whole-object pair it replaced was wrong. There is\ndeliberately no `SEARCH` counterpart: search is the enumeration primitive\nover a band directory, and `allowBandMemberSearchBands` already says who\nmay have it.",
          "effect": "allow",
          "fields": [
            "Name"
          ],
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedReadBandName",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "BandMemberPolicy",
      "object": "BandMember",
      "rules": [
        {
          "action": "search",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandMemberSearchMembers",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandMember"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandMemberReadMembers",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandMember"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "condition": "User == RUNTIME.userId",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedReadOwnMembership",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "create",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminCreateMembers",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "update",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminUpdateMembers",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "delete",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminDeleteMembers",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "BandInvitationPolicy",
      "object": "BandInvitation",
      "rules": [
        {
          "action": "create",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminCreateInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminReadInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "condition": "Invitee == RUNTIME.userId",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowInviteeReadOwnInvitation",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "search",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminSearchInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "search",
          "comment": "Deliberately unconditioned, mirroring Jointly Care's\n`CircleInvitePolicy.allowAuthenticatedSearchInvites` and this app's own\n`AvailabilityPolicy.allowAuthenticatedSearchAvailability`: a `SEARCH`\nrule's `WHEN` is evaluated against `request.record`, which the coarse\n\"may this principal search this object at all\" gate never has, so\n`Invitee == RUNTIME.userId` here would test a condition against no record\nand could never grant anything. The compiler names that shape\n(`ADL_POLICY_CONTEXT_MEMBER_SEARCH_UNREACHABLE`) for the principal that\ncannot express it at all.\n\nThis does not open a directory, and two independent gates are why.\n`requireObjectScopeForSearch` narrows to `getAllowedContextIds` before any\nrecord is read, so an invitee reaches only the bands a `pendingBand\nInvitation` grant admits them to; then `ObjectStore.search` filters every\nsurviving result through the per-record read rules, where\n`allowInviteeReadOwnInvitation` (`WHEN Invitee == RUNTIME.userId`) is the\nonly rule a non-admin matches. A `BandAdmin` still sees their own band's\ninvitations and nobody else's, by the same two gates.\n\nWithout it, `MyBandInvitations` throws `Policy denied search on object\n'BandInvitation'` for exactly the caller it exists for: `ReadModelService.\nsearchAuthorisedSourceRecords` checks `search` first, before any scope or\nper-record filtering, so `allowBandAdminSearchInvitations` alone made an\ninvitee's own invitation unreachable through every read model over this\nobject.",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedSearchInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "update",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminUpdateInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "update",
          "condition": "(Invitee == RUNTIME.userId) AND (Status == 'Accepted')",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowInviteeAcceptInvitation",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "update",
          "condition": "(Invitee == RUNTIME.userId) AND (Status == 'Accepted')",
          "effect": "deny",
          "fields": [
            "Band",
            "Inviter",
            "Invitee",
            "InviteeEmail",
            "Role"
          ],
          "name": "denyInviteeIdentityInvitationUpdates",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated"
          }
        },
        {
          "action": "delete",
          "effect": "allow",
          "name": "allowBandAdminDeleteInvitations",
          "principal": {
            "match": "specific",
            "roles": [
              "BandAdmin"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
