        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "The admin-facing counterpart to `PendingInvitations`: every invitation this\nband has sent, in any status, so a `BandAdmin` can see what was accepted,\ndeclined or revoked as well as what is still outstanding. `IsSender` uses\nthe same `runtime.userId` comparison the object's own policy rules already\nuse for `Invitee` (see `BandInvitationPolicy.allowInviteeReadOwnInvitation`)\nso the view can tell an admin which invitations they personally sent.",
      "context": {
        "context": "Band",
        "mode": "required"
      },
      "fields": [
        {
          "comment": "`InviteeEmail` leads the field list on purpose: the generic dashboard\nrenderer used by a `READ_MODEL`-backed view with no composed presentation\n(see `MyInvitationList` in `ui.adlj`, and `BandMemberAvailabilityBoard` /\n`SetListByPosition` for the same pattern elsewhere in this app) always\nshows every read-model field, using the first non-date field as each\nrow's bold title -- so `Inviter` (a lookup id, not something to read)\ncomes last, alongside the `IsSender` field it only exists to support.",
          "field": "InviteeEmail",
          "name": "InviteeEmail",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "Role",
          "name": "Role",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "Status",
          "name": "Status",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "SentAt",
          "name": "SentAt",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "RespondedAt",
          "name": "RespondedAt",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "Inviter",
          "name": "Inviter",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "expression": "Inviter == RUNTIME.userId",
          "name": "IsSender",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      ],
      "name": "SentBandInvitations",
      "sort": [
        {
          "direction": "desc",
          "field": "SentAt"
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "invitation",
          "object": "BandInvitation",
          "scope": "currentContext"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "The invitee-facing counterpart to `PendingInvitations` and\n`SentBandInvitations`, which are both `CONTEXT REQUIRED Band` and so can\nonly be opened by somebody who has already picked a band -- which an\ninvited musician has no reason to do, and until Phase 105 no way to\nbenefit from. `CONTEXT ALL` plus `SCOPE allAvailableContexts` reaches\nevery band the caller can get to *including* the ones only a\n`pendingBandInvitation` grant admits them to, so a person who belongs to\nnothing still has somewhere their invitation appears.\n\nUnlike Jointly Care's `MyPendingCircleInvites`, this one does name the\nband: `BandPolicy.allowAuthenticatedReadBandName` grants `Band.Name` as a\nfield and never the record, so `Band`'s own `LOOKUP Band DISPLAY Name`\nresolves to \"The Betas\" rather than degrading to the stored id.\n\nThis is deliberately not filtered to `Status == 'Pending'`. The read model\nis what a caller may *see*; which rows carry an `Accept` button is the\nview's business, and `MyBandInvitationList` states it as a list `FILTER`\nbeside the action's own `WHEN`.",
      "context": {
        "context": "Band",
        "mode": "all"
      },
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "Band",
          "name": "Band",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "Role",
          "name": "Role",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "Status",
          "name": "Status",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "field": "SentAt",
          "name": "SentAt",
          "source": "invitation"
        },
        {
          "comment": "Projected so the view's row `ACTION` can gate itself to the row's\nactual invitee. `allowAuthenticatedSearchInvitations` is\nunconditioned and `allowBandAdminReadInvitations` legitimately lets an\nadmin read every invitation their own band sent, so this read model\nalso surfaces an admin's own outgoing invitations -- rows they are\nnever the `Invitee` of. `AcceptBandInvitation`'s own `REQUIRE Invitee\n== RUNTIME.userId` step guard makes offering the button on somebody\nelse's invitation safe either way, but a button that always fails for\nthe person looking at it is still worth not drawing.",
          "field": "Invitee",
          "name": "Invitee",
          "source": "invitation"
        }
      ],
      "name": "MyBandInvitations",
      "sort": [
        {
          "direction": "asc",
          "field": "SentAt"
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "invitation",
          "object": "BandInvitation",
          "scope": "allAvailableContexts"
        }
      ]
    }
